# Release-build artifacts (generated fresh by release.yml, never committed)
/latest.json
/SHA256SUMS.txt

# Belt and braces: `src-tauri/.gitignore` already ignores `/target/`, and that
# nested file is the *only* thing keeping Tailwind's source scan out of it.
# Tailwind's walk honours .gitignore, and `src-tauri/target` here is ~100 GB
# across ~195k files — so if that one line were ever removed or negated, a
# six-second production build would become an unbounded one. Naming it here too
# means the guard does not depend on a single line in a nested file.
src-tauri/target/

# Audit reports. Written by a review pass, kept out of the tree on purpose: a
# list of a codebase's unfixed weaknesses — its SSRF guard, its OAuth listener,
# its IPC surface, its token stores — is a map for anyone who reads the repo,
# and this one is public. What such a pass concludes belongs in CLAUDE.md (the
# invariants) and ROADMAP.md (what is left), which is where the last one's
# findings went.
/audit/
